{"name":"Evergreen Fog","hex":"#95978a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"evergreen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of plants, especially trees, that do not shed their leaves seasonally.","Continually fresh or self-renewing.\n Being a clause which causes an automatic renewal of a contract unless action is taken.\n Of a document, a piece of software, or a data set: kept continually up to date (as opposed to being published at regular intervals and outdated in the meantime)"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub or tree that does not shed its leaves or needles seasonally.","A conifer tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evergreen"},{"term":"fog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick cloud that forms near the ground; the obscurity of such a cloud.","A mist or film clouding a surface."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become covered with or as if with fog.","To become obscured in condensation or water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fog"}],"entries":[{"title":"Evergreen","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, an evergreen is a plant which has foliage that remains green and functional throughout the year. This contrasts with deciduous plants, which lose their foliage completely during the winter or dry season. Consisting of many different species, the unique feature of evergreen plants lends itself to various environments and purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Abies_alba_02.jpg/330px-Abies_alba_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evergreen","wikidata":"Q190489"},{"title":"Fog","blocks":[{"text":"Fog is a visible aerosol consisting of tiny water droplets or ice crystals held in the air near the Earth's surface. Fog can be considered a type of low-lying cloud usually resembling stratus and is heavily influenced by nearby bodies of water, topography, and wind conditions. In turn, fog affects many human activities, such as shipping, travel, and warfare. Recent atmospheric research indicates that fog also functions as an active aquatic ecosystem. Fog droplets harbor microbiomes where bacteria actively grow, divide, and interact with atmospheric chemistry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg/330px-A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fog","wikidata":"Q37477"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A3%CE%B1%CE%BC%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.jpg/500px-%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A3%CE%B1%CE%BC%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A3%CE%B1%CE%BC%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.jpg/1280px-%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A3%CE%B1%CE%BC%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A3%CE%B1%CE%BC%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.jpg/500px-%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A3%CE%B1%CE%BC%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cupressus sempervirens (Mediterranean cypress), an evergreen tree","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A